# ffmpeg sources fetched on demand by scripts/build-ffmpeg.sh.
# Each source tree is hundreds of MB; never commit.
sources/
build/

# Cargo build outputs for this crate's compile (not the staged dist/).
target/

# dist/ is DELIBERATELY NOT IGNORED.
#
# This crate's contract is that the static archives are present: build.rs
# panics rather than falling back on a system ffmpeg, so a consumer that
# resolves this crate from a git tag gets a checkout it cannot build unless
# dist/ is committed. A cargo git checkout is not a place a build script can
# be run, so "run scripts/build-ffmpeg.sh first" is not available to them.
#
# This file previously carried that reasoning as a comment and then ignored
# dist/ on the next line, which is how the tagged releases came to contain no
# archives at all.
#
# To rebuild from source (bumping ffmpeg-version.txt, changing the configure
# flags), run scripts/build-ffmpeg.sh and commit the regenerated dist/.
